# THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt records a sha256 of each input over the bytes on disk, and
# src/lib/third-party-licenses.test.ts and the release workflow recompute them. Git's default
# core.autocrlf=true on Windows (the owner's machine and the Windows runner) would convert every
# input to CRLF and stale all of them at once; eol=lf overrides it.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png -text
*.ico -text
*.icns -text
